      <h2 id="view-project-dashboards_odc-monitoring-project-and-application-metrics-using-developer-perspective" class="group scroll-mt-20">Viewing project dashboards<a href="#view-project-dashboards_odc-monitoring-project-and-application-metrics-using-developer-perspective" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">View pre-built dashboards showing CPU usage, memory usage, bandwidth consumption, and network information across your project (namespace) topology to help you monitor application performance.</p>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>In the <strong>Developer</strong> perspective navigation menu, select <strong>Observe</strong>.</li>
      <li>Select a project from the <strong>Project</strong> list. After you select a project, the monitoring tabs are displayed.</li>
      <li>
      Click the <strong>Dashboards</strong> tab.
      <p>The <strong>Dashboards</strong> tab displays pre-built Kubernetes compute resources dashboards showing metrics such as CPU usage, memory usage, bandwidth consumption, and network-related information. The dashboard layout includes metric cards at the top showing current utilization percentages, and expandable graph sections below showing detailed resource usage trends over time.</p>
      </li>
      </ol>
      <h2 id="odc-monitoring-your-application-metrics_odc-monitoring-project-and-application-metrics-using-developer-perspective" class="group scroll-mt-20">Monitoring your application metrics<a href="#odc-monitoring-your-application-metrics_odc-monitoring-project-and-application-metrics-using-developer-perspective" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">Inspect alerts, metric charts, and health check status for individual application workloads to troubleshoot performance issues and monitor health directly from the topology view.</p>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
